11. two gaps in the harness itself, found while extending it
================================================================================
  Both were found by making a check that could only ever pass, fail.

  (a) the rewritten script still read /proc/$gxp for the gx_fpd uid, because rewrite() enumerated the
      variables to move (/proc/$H, /proc/$_pid) and $gxp was not in the list. On the host /proc/7777
      does not exist, so the uid came out EMPTY and the scenario still passed -- the branch ran, the
      answer was vacuous. The fix is a landed check that counts instead of spot-checking:
          all=$(grep -o '/proc/\$' "$s" | wc -l); moved=$(grep -oF "$FR/proc/\$" "$s" | wc -l)
      and refuses to run if they differ. It immediately found a SECOND one: the rule for /proc/$A was
      a no-op (`s#/proc/\$A#/proc/\$A#g`), so the HAL-vs-container mount-namespace comparison read two
      nonexistent paths, got two empty strings, and reported "same mount namespace" for the wrong
      reason. Both are now real paths, and section 9 drives the differing case.

  (b) `notwant '^systemctl restart (?!lomiri-location-service)'` used a PCRE lookahead in an ERE
      pattern, so it matched nothing and passed vacuously. Replaced with a count: exactly one restart.

================================================================================
12. what this round does NOT show
================================================================================
  * Nothing about the device. It is in EDL; every container property, module listing, /proc walk and
    logcat count in the probe is a FIXTURE. The device answers are still owed.
  * The chain above is read out of the VENDOR IMAGE, which is a file, and it is the same image the
    device runs -- but "the module is on disk" is not "the module loaded".
  * Which of the two stores is the one that actually fails on the device is NOT decided here. The
    wrapper's access() gate is the first silent failure and the only one with evidence (docs 83);
    /data/gf_data, the gx_fpd hop and the logcat counts are the three candidates BEHIND it, and the
    probe now measures all three separately instead of assuming the first explains the rest.
